{"type":"text","timestamp":1787413407213,"sessionID":"ses_fd5de0bedffeII2FwqH8SyHTad","part":{"id":"prt_02a241e16001ovXdPlB30lWljE","messageID":"msg_02a23fa26001cieSAMY3ReW9nl","sessionID":"ses_fd5de0bedffeII2FwqH8SyHTad","type":"text","text":"My probe test was incorrect — the contract specifies `ignore` is a glob or array of globs, not a matcher function. The earlier test already proved isolation: with an ignored input, `onResult` fired exactly 3 times (not 4), confirming the ignore matcher did not inherit the caller's callbacks. Array patterns and callbacks work correctly. Let me confirm with a valid glob probe:","time":{"start":1787413405206,"end":1787413407207}}}
