{"type":"text","timestamp":1787413417074,"sessionID":"ses_fd5de0bedffeII2FwqH8SyHTad","part":{"id":"prt_02a2443df001llOYhtrp0CgEE6","messageID":"msg_02a243722001xxsLPZCvM8cJ6u","sessionID":"ses_fd5de0bedffeII2FwqH8SyHTad","type":"text","text":"Done. Changes are confined to `lib/glob-match.js`.\n\nSummary of what I added:\n- `applyOutcome` helper that resolves the final decision and fires lifecycle callbacks.\n- `ignore`: builds a separate matcher (with caller callbacks/ignore stripped) so ignore patterns never inherit the caller's callbacks; a pattern match that also matches ignore becomes a non-match (`isMatch: false`, `isIgnored: true`, `onIgnore` fires, `onMatch` does not).\n- `onResult`/`onMatch`/`onIgnore` callbacks invoked once per input with the result object (`glob`, `regex`, `input`, `output`, `isMatch` + extras).\n- Inputs that never matched the pattern are reported as non-match with no `onIgnore`.\n- Array patterns: callbacks/ignore applied once at the array level (sub-matchers recurse with them stripped); existing boolean and `returnObject` behavior preserved.\n- The 5 pre-existing test failures exist on the base commit and are unrelated to this change.","time":{"start":1787413414879,"end":1787413417038}}}
